# Toma = website recap, not a VO script

When writing or changing the jornada Toma (`/toma`, `jornadaTakeAi`, the paper board), read and follow:

`doc/ACCESO_FUTBOL_SCRIPT_GUIDE.md`

Use **Section 4** (website J4 recap) plus **Section 0** with the website exception.

## Apply
- Accents ON in website copy (`análisis`, `Selección`). The no-accent rule is VO/graphics only.
- No em-dashes. Period or comma.
- First-person take (`yo creo` / `honestamente` / `para mí`) in the column.
- At least one verified stat from the dossier (Sportmonks / cable). Never invent scores.
- Headline max 8 words. Dek is one short line (window + how many games). Column is 2 grafs: tabla, then the take + dividing question. Never a partido-por-partido rundown — that is Dónde ver.
- Spoken clocks only in Toma copy: `lunes a las nueve de la noche`, `Pachuca contra Puebla`. Never `9:06 p.m. (PAC–PUE)`.
- Print **Liga MX** with a space. TTS says `Liga eme equis`. Never write `LigaMX` in Toma copy.
- Standings: Apertura 2026 corte is **top 8, no Play-In** (product override of the guide's Play-In line).
- Close with a dividing question (binary or A/B/C), not "síguenos."
- Blocklist as standalone hook: Márquez appointment, Almada arrival, Gignac departure, "Atlante regresó."

## Do not apply (VO-only)
- `Preparense que arrancamos`
- Stripping vowel accents
- TikTok runtime / hashtag packaging

# Audio Toma episodes (`src/lib/toma/`)

The ElevenLabs episode is a different format from the column above. `writeTomaNarration` writes from `buildTomaNarrationFacts` (live tabla, jornadas restantes, 2–3 "qué ver" picks with derby name, MX + US Central kickoff, venue, TV, H2H, form). The column is tone only.
- Hook = a number plus a consequence. Never open with "Mira" or an abstract line.
- Every number comes from the facts pack. Gaps, places and streaks are pre-worded (`frase`, `tabla`, `forma`, `siGana`) so the model never does table math. Unverified point totals trigger a retry, then no episode.
- Fan names and derbies: Chivas, Rayados, Xolos; Clásico Tapatío / Nacional / Joven / Capitalino / Regio (`narrationFacts.ts`).
- Picks name day, spoken time in Mexico and US Central, one or two facts and one consequence. Not the full slate.
- Filler blocklist lives in `FILLER` in `writeDialogue.ts`; extend it rather than loosening the prompt.
- Close: "¿Quién se lleva X? A o B, comenta." then `tomaOutro(kind)` (sign-off + follow line), appended in code.
- The model also returns a page `headline` + `subhead`; the episode page uses those, never the transcript's first lines.
- Bump `TOMA_VOICE_REV` when the voice or format changes so stored episodes regenerate.
